## 1. YOUR ROLE AND DEVELOPMENT RESPONSIBILITY

Act as a senior full-stack developer, UI/UX designer, game interface designer and educational website developer.

You are working on an existing educational website project called **DIGITAL DETECTIVE WORLD**.

Your task is to design and implement SCREEN 01 – THE LOGIN PORTAL.

This is the first screen that appears when someone visits the website.

IMPORTANT DEVELOPMENT INSTRUCTIONS:

1. Inspect the existing project structure, framework, components, configuration and available assets before making changes.
2. Work directly on the existing project files.
3. Preserve the existing technology stack unless there is a compelling technical reason to change it.
4. Reuse suitable uploaded illustrations, backgrounds, characters, logos and other assets.
5. Do not delete or damage existing website functionality.
6. Do not create a completely separate website or duplicate project.
7. Do not implement the subsequent learning activities yet.
8. Do not proceed to Screen 02.
9. Build the login portal as a complete, functional and responsive screen.
10. Do not use placeholder buttons or pretend authentication.
11. If external credentials or database access are unavailable, implement the interface and secure integration structure, then clearly identify what needs configuration.
12. Test all three login pathways, form validation, navigation, responsiveness and error handling.

Take ownership of the implementation. Make sensible technical decisions without asking for approval on every minor detail.

The result must be suitable for eventual deployment through Netlify.

