## 5.5 Student authentication behaviour

Authenticate using the combination of:

- Class Code.
- Student ID.
- Student PIN.

IMPORTANT TECHNICAL REQUIREMENT:

The student login must be implemented securely.

Do not authenticate students by simply comparing PINs against publicly readable database records.

Use a secure server-side authentication flow, such as an appropriately implemented Supabase Edge Function or another secure authentication mechanism.

The backend must:
- Validate the class code.
- Validate the student ID.
- Verify the PIN securely.
- Apply rate limiting.
- Prevent brute-force attempts.
- Create an authenticated student session.
- Return only the necessary student profile information.
- Enforce student role permissions.

Never store student PINs in plain text.

Never expose private authentication credentials in frontend code.

Do not reveal whether a particular student ID or class code exists through detailed error messages.

## 5.6 Student login error messages

Use these exact friendly messages:

EMPTY FIELDS:

"Oops! Please complete your login details."

INCORRECT DETAILS:

"Hmm... That doesn't look right, Detective. Please check your details and try again!"

TOO MANY ATTEMPTS:

"Please wait a moment before trying again."

NETWORK ERROR:

"Oops! We couldn't connect. Please check your internet connection and try again."

Do not expose technical error messages to pupils.

## 5.7 Successful student login

After successful authentication:

FIRST-TIME STUDENT:

- Create the student session.
- Check whether an avatar has already been created.
- If no avatar exists, proceed to the Avatar Creation Screen.
- Save the completed avatar to the student's profile.
- Continue to Screen 02.

RETURNING STUDENT:

- Restore the saved avatar.
- Restore the player's previous XP.
- Restore stars and badges.
- Restore completed missions.
- Restore the last saved learning position.
- Continue to Screen 02 or the appropriate saved learning position according to the website's resume design.

Display the following success message:

"Welcome back, Detective! Your adventure is waiting!"

Use a smooth, cheerful transition.

IMPORTANT:
Do not build the avatar creation screen or Detective Pusheen's full welcome scene as part of Screen 01. Those belong to the next screen.

